==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|gunþiz|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|gʷʰéntis|killing, blow|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|gʷʰen-|hit, drive|lang=|title=}}. Cognate with Old Saxon ''[[gudea|gūdea]]'', Old High German ''gund-'' (in ''[[gundfano]]'' ‘war-flag’), Old Norse ''[[guðr]], [[gunnr]]''. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin ''[[defendo|defendere]]'' and ''[[offendo|offendere]]'', Slavic ''*gъnati-'' (Old Church Slavonic [[гънати]], Russian [[гнать]]), Avestan {{term|𐬘𐬀𐬌𐬥𐬙𐬌|sc=Avst||to kill|tr=jainti}}, Sanskrit {{term|हन्ति|tr=hanti||to slay|lang=sa}}, Baltic ''*giñ-'' (Lithuanian ''[[giñti]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡuːθ/|lang=ang}}

